I disagree. My first ascension was a wizard who started off that
way. My experience suggests that relying too heavily on spellcasting in
the early game leads to a lot of deaths with empty power. I'd rather be 
able to run from a mumak and then still able to run from another mumak
then be able to kill the first one but have no power left to take out 
the second. 

That said, it does depend on playing style; if you flee a lot and are
careful with Elbereth, you don't need the body armor, and not carrying
a dagger stack lets you carry other useful objects. As I tend to turn
the corner into all sorts of nasty things because I am holding down 
motion keys, I find body armor crucial in the early game, and don't 
turn to spellcasting until much later, whether I am playing a Wizard 
or a Barbarian.

